## 5. Context rules

{{#ctx_code_product}}
- **Product code:** changes reach protected branches only through an approved PR with green required checks; give extra scrutiny to [fill in: safety-related and security-sensitive code named in the development plan].
{{/ctx_code_product}}
{{#ctx_code_tooling}}
- **Internal tooling:** same review rules; tooling that produces QMS records or verification results is validated before its output is used as evidence.
{{/ctx_code_tooling}}
{{#ctx_pr_review}}
- **AI PR review:** advisory only; never the required approval and never the only review.
{{/ctx_pr_review}}
{{#ctx_test_generation}}
- **Test generation:** generated tests trace to the requirement they verify and are reviewed like product code.
{{/ctx_test_generation}}
{{#ctx_doc_drafting}}
- **Document drafting:** every factual statement cites a source you check yourself; you preview the exact content before anything is written to a controlled record; the document owner approves under document control.
{{/ctx_doc_drafting}}
{{#ctx_agents_qms}}
- **QMS agents:** only configured agents, only on their declared write targets; agent outputs that change records require confirmation by the accountable role.
{{/ctx_agents_qms}}

